        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ca303981-2754-54c4-89ef-33f66663d457",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hal B. Wallis, Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, Sylvia Sidney, Bette Davis, Errol Flynn\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Films: Casablanca, True Grit, The Maltese Falcon, The Big Sleep, Dead End\n- Topics: American film production, film noir, screen and stage acting\n\nFacts:\n- Hal B. Wallis, born Aaron Blum Wolowicz on October 19, 1898, was an American film producer.\n- Humphrey Bogart, born on December 25, 1899 and died on January 14, 1957, was an American screen and stage actor.\n- The 1937 film Dead End stars Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, and Sylvia Sidney.\n- Humphrey Bogart became a cultural icon through his performances in 1940s film noir films such as The Maltese Falcon, Casablanca, and The Big Sleep.\n- Hal B. Wallis is best remembered for producing Casablanca in 1942 and many other major films for Warner Bros. featuring stars such as Humphrey Bogart, Bette Davis, and Errol Flynn.\n- Hal B. Wallis also produced True Grit in 1969.\n- Hal B. Wallis died on October 5, 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "15089495-05c6-5dc3-b706-5e2d25150a7d",
        "text": "Page: Hal B. Wallis. Sentence: Harold Brent Wallis (born Aaron Blum Wolowicz; October 19, 1898 – October 5, 1986) was an American film producer.\nPage: Hal B. Wallis. Sentence: He is best remembered for producing \"Casablanca\" (1942) and \"True Grit\" (1969), along with many other major films for Warner Bros. featuring such film stars as Humphrey Bogart, Bette Davis, and Errol Flynn.\nPage: Humphrey Bogart. Sentence: Humphrey DeForest Bogart ( ; December 25, 1899January 14, 1957) was an American screen and stage actor whose performances in 1940s films noir such as \"The Maltese Falcon\", \"Casablanca\", and \"The Big Sleep\" earned him status as a cultural icon.\nPage: Dead End (1937 film). Sentence: It stars Humphrey Bogart, Joel McCrea, and Sylvia Sidney.",
